clickT -- the mock click, G2 stroke 3 and goal G1 (Tony, 2026-11-13). Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh.
click(request) names a form and a field: it selects the field, fires the field's own action, then its attribute actions
left to right. firstLight's ok holds onClick:=okClick, which writes insideForm; insideForm's listener redraws.

Each page is read at heading's wall (300,15), a point low in the held form (200,390), and ok's green (390,190).
CK-1  before: no listener run; (200,390) is the descriptions form's lightGreen.
CK-2  THE CLICK: ok is selected, its onClick fired okClick, one listener run; (200,390) is okNote's white and its text is drawn.
CK-3  a second click brings descriptions back: two runs, and the page is CK-1's by value.
CK-4  a field with no action (heading): selected, nothing fired, no listener run.
CK-5  a name the form has no field for, and a request with no field name: each refused by name; nothing selected anew, no run.
CK-6  ORDER: ckOwn has its own action and two attribute actions with a plain attribute between them; the order digit by
      digit is 1 (own), 2 (first), 3 (second): 123.
H7: with the attribute loop's fire line removed, CK-2 and CK-3 show no swap and CK-6 reads 1.
